From 590daf6cd01f9b24d16e389b30a8ffc303471593 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wine-thumbs <wine-thumbs@localhost>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 20:56:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] shell32: Fix the background menu and remember the sort
 order of each folder.

The View, Arrange Icons and New submenus of the background context menu
had ids outside of the FCIDM_BASE range, so merging the menu dropped them,
and the commands that remained were forwarded to the view with the merge
offset still applied. The submenus now use ids in that range and the
view gets the real command ids; the current view mode and sort order are
marked, and Auto Arrange and Line up Icons work.

Arrange Icons gains Ascending and Descending. The column and direction a
folder is sorted by are kept per folder (HKCU\Software\Wine\Shell\
FolderSort) and restored when the folder is shown again, in every view
mode, and the details view header shows the sort arrow. Dates and sizes
start with the newest and biggest, names sort naturally ("2" before
"10") and file sizes no longer overflow the comparison.
